4. Why the Google Sign-In Popup Fails in Your /u/1/ AI Studio Tab
Separate /u/0/ and /u/1/ AI Studio editor tabs stay isolated because the /u/1/ prefix stays in the URL bar, but the Google Sign-In popup routes through the unprefixed *.run.app preview origin and Google's AI Studio proxy resolves *.run.app requests under /u/0/.
That account mismatch causes the popup to hit https://aistudio.google.com/404 (whose Go to library button defaults back to /u/0/), and security headers on that page hide its window handle from the opener tab so ExoNovel reports "OAuth popup was closed. Please try again." even though the window stayed open.
Live production (https://exonovel.exosystems.net) runs directly on your own domain without the AI Studio proxy and is unaffected. For local preview testing in that tab, sign in with Email and Password, or open ExoNovel in a separate browser profile or container where exonomyapp@gmail.com is the primary /u/0/ Google account.
